{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md | sed -n '397,490p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py | sed -n '224,295p'; ls docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid | sort\"","aggregated_output":"   397\t### Council I (`council-i-codex.md`, DISAGREE) and the amendment, written before any fresh mark was opened\n   398\t**Verified.** The pool held questions the design had read under another label or in another draw. Examples:\n   399\t- old-1 Q8 is the same FY2027 data-center revenue question as the exposed old-2 Q9, word for word;\n   400\t- the same holds for FY2027 gross margin, FY2028 gross margin, and two OpenAI chip-financing questions.\n   401\t\n   402\tClaude's own reflection (`council-i-claude.md`) had called this mild. It is not: the census looked at these questions.\n   403\t\n   404\t**Amended rule:**\n   405\t- **Bets.** Each pooled question gets a bet, read by Claude from its text against the 73 questions the design read\n   406\t  (`fresh-bets.json`). The file was written before any fresh mark was opened.\n   407\t  - 52 answers sit on a bet the design read, and are excluded.\n   408\t  - Questions that are the same bet across draws share one label. **Each bet gives at most one case**: from its answers in seeded\n   409\t    order, the first rejected one becomes a target; otherwise the first supported one becomes a control candidate.\n   410\t  - Bets the frozen matter list keeps apart stay apart: 2026 capex (M04) is not the exposed 2027 capex (M14). A bet adjacent to an\n   411\t    exposed one is excluded: stand-alone CPU revenue next to total CPU revenue, and AI-buildout bond issuance next to the\n   412\t    bond-issuance share.\n   413\t- **Prerequisites enforced in code before any send:**\n   414\t  - n ≥ 8 targets;\n   415\t  - ceil(8n/13) controls;\n   416\t  - all 3 census plants rejected by both readers.\n   417\t\n   418\t  Otherwise there is no send, and the shortfall goes back to the council.\n   419\t- **Scoring.**\n   420\t  - A production refusal counts as not supported.\n   421\t  - A plant the readers do not reject voids the reading.\n   422\t  - Rung moves are reported as a description only. The falsifier on moves stays a description, not a gate.\n   423\t- **H2 is not sent.** One account in 24 is too little, and \"this evidence\" could be read to leave out the dependencies and themes. It\n   424\t  is parked with that reason. Claude agrees: the cheaper course.\n   224\t    \"\"\"The comparison's readers (jp.read), with the brief's date set to the cut: the cards show the library as it stood on 6 September.\"\"\"\n   225\t    sys.path[:0] = [str(jp.STAGE0), str(jp.STAGE0 / 'census')]\n   226\t    import mark_cards\n   227\t    brief, count = re.subn(r'as it stood on 20\\nSeptember 2026', 'as it stood on 6\\nSeptember 2026', mark_cards.BRIEF)\n   228\t    assert count == 1, 'the brief names the cut date once'\n   229\t    mark_cards.BRIEF = brief\n   230\t    jp.read(deck, key_path, marks_name)\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\tdef rejected(mark):\n   234\t    answer = (mark or {}).get('answer')\n   235\t    if isinstance(answer, dict):\n   236\t        return set(answer['split']) <= REJECTED\n   237\t    return answer in REJECTED\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\tdef select():\n   241\t    \"\"\"The rule in DESIGN-J2.md (\"The fresh test\", amended by council I), written before any fresh mark was opened. Each pooled question\n   242\t    has a bet (fresh-bets.json); a bet the design read is excluded, and each remaining bet yields at most one case, from its answers in\n   243\t    seeded order: a target when any answer is rejected by both readers on a question both rate worth tracking (the first such), else a\n   244\t    control candidate (the first answer both support on a worth-tracking question). Controls: ceil(8n/13) candidates matched to the\n   245\t    targets by type, seeded. Refused unless n >= 8, the controls are complete and every plant is unsupported by both readers.\"\"\"\n   246\t    marks = json.loads((jp.OUT / 'marks-fresh-census.json').read_text())\n   247\t    rows = {c['case']: c for c in json.loads(POOL.read_text())}\n   248\t    bets = json.loads((HERE / 'fresh-bets.json').read_text())['bets']\n   249\t    assert set(bets) == set(rows), 'every pooled answer has a bet'\n   250\t    by_case = {m['case']: m['marks'] for m in marks.values() if m['kind'] == 'stored'}\n   251\t    missing = [c for c in rows if c not in by_case]\n   252\t    if missing:\n   253\t        raise SystemExit(f'{len(missing)} pooled answers not marked: refused')\n   254\t    plants = {cid: m['marks'] for cid, m in marks.items() if m['kind'] == 'plant'}\n   255\t    plants_caught = all((m or {}).get('answer') in REJECTED or rejected(m) for m in plants.values())\n   256\t    worth = {c for c, m in by_case.items() if m.get('worth') == 'worth'}\n   257\t    rng = random.Random(jp.SEED)\n   258\t    groups = {}\n   259\t    for case in sorted(rows):\n   260\t        if not bets[case].startswith('exposed:'):\n   261\t            groups.setdefault(bets[case], []).append(case)\n   262\t    targets, candidates = [], []\n   263\t    for bet in sorted(groups):\n   264\t        order = rng.sample(groups[bet], len(groups[bet]))\n   265\t        hit = next((c for c in order if c in worth and rejected(by_case[c])), None)\n   266\t        if hit:\n   267\t            targets.append(hit)\n   268\t            continue\n   269\t        good = next((c for c in order if c in worth and by_case[c].get('answer') == 'supported'), None)\n   270\t        if good:\n   271\t            candidates.append(good)\n   272\t    need = math.ceil(8 * len(targets) / 13)\n   273\t    controls = []\n   274\t    for t in targets:\n   275\t        if len(controls) >= need:\n   276\t            break\n   277\t        free = [c for c in candidates if c not in controls and rows[c]['type'] == rows[t]['type']] or [c for c in candidates if c not in controls]\n   278\t        if free:\n   279\t            controls.append(rng.choice(free))\n   280\t    print(f'bets: {len(groups)} fresh of {len(set(bets.values()))}; worth-tracking answers {len(worth)} of {len(rows)}; targets {len(targets)} '\n   281\t          f'(held the previous rung: {sum(rows[t][\"held\"] for t in targets)}); control candidates {len(candidates)}; controls {len(controls)} of {need}; '\n   282\t          f'screen: net repairs >= {math.ceil(5 * len(targets) / 13)}; plants caught: {plants_caught} {plants}')\n   283\t    print('targets', [(t, bets[t]) for t in targets])\n   284\t    if len(targets) < 8 or len(controls) < need or not plants_caught:\n   285\t        raise SystemExit('refused: the prerequisites of the fresh test are not met (n >= 8, controls complete, plants caught); no send')\n   286\t    out = [dict(rows[c], role='target', bet=bets[c], mark=by_case[c]) for c in targets] + \\\n   287\t          [dict(rows[c], role='control', bet=bets[c], mark=by_case[c]) for c in controls]\n   288\t    FRESH.write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   289\t\n   290\t\n   291\tdef check(path=FRESH):\n   292\t    \"\"\"$0: for every fresh case and arm, the request is built; the heading is replaced exactly once in H1 and H2 and nowhere else; the\n   293\t    v7 request equals the stored bytes; a synthetic answer (the stored one) passes the production check against each arm's request.\"\"\"\n   294\t    from hivemind import model\n   295\t    rows = json.loads(path.read_text())\nDESIGN-J2.md\nPLAN.md\n__pycache__\narms\ncensus\ncouncil-a-brief.md\ncouncil-a-codex.md\ncouncil-a-codex.stream\ncouncil-b-brief.md\ncouncil-b-codex.md\ncouncil-b-codex.stream\ncouncil-c-brief.md\ncouncil-c-codex.md\ncouncil-c-codex.stream\ncouncil-d-brief.md\ncouncil-d-codex.md\ncouncil-d-codex.stream\ncouncil-e-brief.md\ncouncil-e-codex.md\ncouncil-e-codex.stream\ncouncil-f-brief.md\ncouncil-f-codex.md\ncouncil-f-codex.stream\ncouncil-g-brief.md\ncouncil-g-codex.md\ncouncil-g-codex.stream\ncouncil-h-brief.md\ncouncil-h-codex.md\ncouncil-h-codex.stream\ncouncil-i-brief.md\ncouncil-i-claude.md\ncouncil-i-codex.md\ncouncil-i-codex.stream\ncouncil-j-brief.md\ncouncil-j-codex.md\ncouncil-j-codex.stream\nfresh-bets.json\nfresh_test.py\njudge_probe.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,collections; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import fresh_test as f; p=f.jp; m={v[\\\"case\\\"]:(k,v[\\\"marks\\\"]) for k,v in json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"marks-fresh-census.json\\\").read_text()).items() if v[\\\"kind\\\"]==\\\"stored\\\"}; pool=json.loads(f.POOL.read_text()); bets=json.loads((f.HERE/\\\"fresh-bets.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"bets\\\"]; metadata=json.loads((p.KEYS/\\\"mapping-key-diagnostic.json\\\").read_text()); qs={(d,r[\\\"question_id\\\"]):r[\\\"question\\\"] for d,l in metadata.items() for r in json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"mapping-out\\\"/(\\\"library-{}.json\\\".format(l))).read_text())}; count=collections.Counter(); numeric=collections.defaultdict(list); flags=[];\nfor c in pool:\n n=c[\\\"case\\\"]; card, mark=m[n]; typ=c[\\\"type\\\"]; bet=bets[n]; cl=\\\"exposed\\\" if bet.startswith(\\\"exposed:\\\") else \\\"fresh\\\"; worth=mark[\\\"worth\\\"]==\\\"worth\\\"; rej=f.rejected(mark); count[cl,typ,\\\"all\\\"]+=1; count[cl,typ,\\\"worth\\\"]+=worth; count[cl,typ,\\\"rejected\\\"]+=rej; count[cl,typ,\\\"rejected and worth\\\"]+=rej and worth;\n if rej: flags.append((card,n,cl,typ,worth,mark,bet,qs[c[\\\"draw\\\"],c[\\\"label\\\"]]));\n if cl==\\\"fresh\\\" and typ==\\\"figure\\\" and worth: numeric[bet].append((n,mark[\\\"answer\\\"],qs[c[\\\"draw\\\"],c[\\\"label\\\"]]));\nprint(\\\"counts\\\",*count.items(),sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\"); print(\\\"rejects\\\",*flags,sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\"); print(\\\"fresh numeric bets worth\\\",len(numeric),*numeric.items(),sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\")'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
