{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,collections; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import fresh_test as f; p=f.jp; fresh=json.loads(f.POOL.read_text()); r=json.loads((p.DIAG/\\\"deck/readings.json\\\").read_text())[\\\"cards\\\"]; paired=[r[c[\\\"draw\\\"]].get(c[\\\"label\\\"],{}) for c in fresh]; print(\\\"09-20 on selected 09-06 pool\\\",sum(bool(m) for m in paired),sum(m.get(\\\"worth\\\")==\\\"worth\\\" for m in paired),sum(m.get(\\\"worth\\\")==\\\"worth\\\" and f.rejected(m) for m in paired));\nfor n in (\\\"T-old-3-Q3\\\",\\\"T-old-3-Q37\\\",\\\"T-old-1-Q7\\\",\\\"C-new-3-Q33\\\",\\\"C-old-2-Q15\\\"):\n for arm in (\\\"v7\\\",\\\"v7-noprev\\\"):\n  a=[json.loads((p.OUT/\\\"probe\\\"/arm/\\\"{}-{}.json\\\".format(n,k)).read_text())[\\\"answer\\\"] for k in (1,2,3)]; print(n,arm,[(x[\\\"rung\\\"],x[\\\"implied_outcome\\\"][:215]) for x in a]);'\"","aggregated_output":"09-20 on selected 09-06 pool 92 56 0\nT-old-3-Q3 v7 [(1, 'About $446 billion: $177.837 billion reported in the first half, roughly $113.6 billion for Q3 using the 3.1% average beat over the high end of guidance, and about $127 billion for Q4 by carrying forward 12% sequent'), (1, 'About $445–446 billion: $177.837 billion in first-half revenue plus roughly $113.6 billion for Q3 using the $108 billion guide and the observed 3.1% average beat over guidance high ends, plus roughly $127 billion fo'), (1, 'Roughly $445 billion: $177.837 billion reported in the first half, about $113.6 billion for Q3 using the $108 billion guide and the observed 3.1% average beat over guidance, and about $127 billion for Q4 carrying fo')]\nT-old-3-Q3 v7-noprev [(2, 'About $410 billion: Q1 and Q2 were $81.62 billion and $96.2 billion; Q3 guidance is $108 billion; and 65% Q4 year-over-year growth applied to an approximately $75 billion FY2026 Q4 baseline implies about $124 billio'), (2, 'About $410 billion: $177.837 billion for the first half (e2754), plus the $108 billion Q3 midpoint (e2715), plus roughly $124 billion for Q4. The Q4 estimate applies the reported 65% growth expectation (e5192) to an'), (2, 'About $405–$411 billion: first-half revenue was $177.8 billion, Q3 is guided at $108 billion (with a specific third-party estimate of $113–$114 billion), and Q4 growth expectations support roughly $114–$120 billion.')]\nT-old-3-Q37 v7 [(3, 'About 72.0% for FY2028: use the bottom of management’s 72%–73% outlook because rising memory costs and tight supply pressure margins, while the negotiated price increases taking effect in Q1 support recovery. No sup'), (3, 'About 72.0%: use the lower end of management’s FY2028 guided range because executed price increases support recovery, while rising memory costs and tight supply weigh against a result above the floor. This is rung 3'), (3, 'About 72.0%, at the guidance range’s lower edge. Executed price increases taking effect in Q1 support recovery, but rising memory costs and persistent supply tightness favor the low end of management’s range.')]\nT-old-3-Q37 v7-noprev [(2, \"About 72.5%, using the midpoint of management's FY2028 guidance of 72%–73%; the forecast already reflects the stated Q4 FY2027 trough and recovery as executed price increases take effect.\"), (2, \"About 72.5% for FY2028: use the midpoint of NVIDIA's 72%–73% guidance, which anticipates recovery as negotiated price increases take effect in Q1. Memory-cost and supply pressures remain downside risks, but the evid\"), (2, 'About 72.5% for FY2028: use the midpoint of the 72%–73% guidance range, with rising memory costs and constrained supply pulling toward its lower end and Q1 FY2028 price increases supporting recovery.')]\nT-old-1-Q7 v7 [(4, \"NVIDIA's $1.3 trillion 2027 forecast for the top five, less roughly $100–$150 billion for Oracle, implies $1.15–$1.20 trillion for these four, centered near $1.17 trillion. That is above rung 4's $1.1 trillion floor\"), (4, 'The $1.3 trillion NVIDIA forecast for the top five hyperscalers, less the carried roughly $100–$150 billion Oracle estimate, implies about $1.15–$1.20 trillion for these four, centered near $1.17 trillion; rung 4.'), (4, \"NVIDIA's $1.3 trillion 2027 estimate for the top five hyperscalers, less roughly $100–$150 billion for Oracle, implies about $1.15–$1.20 trillion for the four in question, centered near $1.17 trillion (rung 4).\")]\nT-old-1-Q7 v7-noprev [(3, \"Approximately $1.05–$1.1 trillion for calendar 2027, within rung 3. The four-company $1.08 trillion consensus is the numerical anchor; NVIDIA's $1.3 trillion estimate is for five hyperscalers and broader capex, so i\"), (3, 'Roughly $1.0 trillion for the four, in rung 3: the four-company Morgan Stanley forecast is over $1 trillion for AI infrastructure (e423), while the $1.08 trillion BofA estimate covers five companies including Oracle'), (3, 'About $1.0–$1.08 trillion for the four companies in scope. The $1.08 trillion consensus is for a broader five-company group, while the explicit forecast for Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta is over $1 trillion; t')]\nC-new-3-Q33 v7 [(4, \"Around $650 billion, but below it: the reported H1 amount exceeds $400 billion, while a rough continuation of August's $42 billion monthly pace for all global venture funding implies less than about $252 billion of \"), (4, \"About $600 billion for calendar 2026, rung 4: NVIDIA's report of more than $400 billion in H1 implies over $800 billion if that pace continued, while August's $42 billion in all-sector venture funding implies roughl\"), (4, \"Near but below $650bn for calendar 2026: start with NVIDIA's claim of more than $400bn in H1, then use the August all-market pace of $42bn/month as roughly $252bn of possible total-market funding over H2; AI is only\")]\nC-new-3-Q33 v7-noprev [(5, 'NVIDIA said AI venture funding exceeded $400 billion in H1 2026. Annualizing that six-month pace implies more than $800 billion for 2026, placing the forecast in rung 5; reaching its $650 billion floor would require'), (5, 'About $800 billion or more for calendar 2026, derived by carrying the reported H1 pace of more than $400 billion through H2. That annualized pace is in rung 5.'), (5, \"NVIDIA's cited H1 2026 total exceeded $400 billion; carrying that six-month funding pace through the calendar year implies more than $800 billion for 2026, before the additional disclosed H2 financings. That run-rat\")]\nC-old-2-Q15 v7 [(5, 'About $215 billion at publication: approximately $187 billion of scheduled commitments remain after the $92 billion FY2027 amount runs off, plus an estimated $28 billion of replenishment to secure supply against exp'), (5, 'About $215 billion at publication: subtract the $92 billion scheduled for the rest of FY2027 from the $279 billion disclosed total to get a $187 billion residual, then add an estimated $28 billion of replenishment. '), (5, 'About $215 billion at publication: the $279 billion disclosed total less $92 billion scheduled for the rest of FY2027 leaves about $187 billion; an estimated roughly $28 billion of replenishment, supported by contin')]\nC-old-2-Q15 v7-noprev [(2, 'About $187 billion on the disclosed schedule: subtract the $92 billion scheduled for the remainder of FY2027 from the $279 billion total, leaving the FY2028-and-later commitments. No quantified evidence supports add'), (5, 'About $187 billion of the disclosed $279 billion schedule falls beyond FY2027 after subtracting the $92 billion scheduled for the rest of FY2027. Given the recent $160 billion increase and continuing demand and supp'), (4, 'About $187 billion: subtract the $92 billion scheduled for the remainder of FY2027 from the $279 billion total, leaving $87 billion for FY2028, $88 billion for FY2029, and $12 billion for FY2030 and later. This is b')]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
